{"id": "EUVD-2026-102531", "enisaUuid": "cdb4fcdc-d14d-3ba4-9776-82cf3f54cf05", "description": "NivoCart through 2.5.1 contains a missing authorization vulnerability in the download() action of account/order that allows unauthenticated attackers to retrieve guest order invoices by supplying an order_id. Attackers can iterate the order_id parameter, which matches guest orders stored with customer_id 0, to disclose guest names, addresses, telephone numbers, emails, purchased items, and totals.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T21:43:22", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T14:36:04", "baseScore": 8.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/nivocart/nivocart/issues/26", "https://github.com/nivocart/nivocart/blob/5bc2c3fc7caed9846b58959183f8ccf599cd4399/upload/catalog/controller/account/order.php#L695-L770", "https://github.com/nivocart/nivocart/blob/5bc2c3fc7caed9846b58959183f8ccf599cd4399/upload/catalog/model/account/order.php#L11-L12", "https://github.com/nivocart/nivocart", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/nivocart-through-2.5.1-guest-order-invoice-disclosure-via-account-order-download"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111277", "GHSA-hpxm-cqxp-f8qc"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.36, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "d69df382-952a-362c-b820-26bf5a3183fe", "product": {"name": "nivocart", "vendor": {"name": "nivocart"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22642.5.1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "892ddbe1-23b6-3289-afc1-a11ac0738d59", "vendor": {"name": "nivocart"}}], "isExploited": false}